r against Austria in the semi-final, the final was the only match that Great Britain was called on to play during the tournament."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the final, Britain scored the first four goals, and led at the half by 5-2. They scored four goals in the second half and shut out Belgium to win, 9-2. The final was a re-match of the " [:a {:href "/results/38000"} "1900 Olympic"] " final, also won by Great Britain over Belgium. Britain’s leading goal scorer, " [:a {:href "/athletes/53957"} "George Wilkinson"] ", had played on the winning team in 1900. For the Belgians, " [:a {:href "/athletes/45499"} "Fernand Feyaerts"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/53499"} "Oscar Grégoire"] " had also played in the 1900 final. Whereas in 1900 the British team had all hailed from Manchester, representing the " [:a {:href "/affiliations/2990"} "Osborne Swimming Club"] ", the 1908 team was a true conglomerate. Three of the players were from the " [:a {:href "/affiliations/3751"} "Salford Swimming Club"] ", two from the " [:a {:href "/affiliations/10031"} "Weston-super-Mare Swimming Club"] ", and one each from " [:a {:href "/affiliations/14711"} "Hyde Seal Swimming Club"] " and Inverness Swim Club."] "\n"] [:button {:id "button131493", :class "btn btn-default"} "Details"] [:script {} "$('#button131493').click(splits)"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {}] [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Team"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Goals"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {:class "accordion-toggle", :data-toggle "collapse", :data-target ".team-members-558193"} [:div {:class "glyphicon glyphicon-plus"}]] [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} "Great Britain"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "9"